-- **10x scale:** add tiered storage per node (RAM + SSD) for large-but-warm values, and isolate “elephant keys” into dedicated shards to keep eviction stable.
-- **100x scale:** push caches closer to edges with a two-level hierarchy (edge cache → regional cache), and formalize namespace-level global invalidation streams (Kafka/PubSub) for correctness-sensitive domains.
+- **10x scale:** add a small edge cache in front of the regional cache to absorb failover cold starts.
+- **100x scale:** isolate “elephant keys” via a separate cache class so large objects don’t dominate eviction.
 
